    "lastText": "All eight issues in ISSUES.md are fixed, and `npm test` passes (10 of 10). I added no new tests, so those 10 are the original ones. I checked the new behaviour with a throwaway script that ran one example from each issue. I didn't check edge cases beyond those.\n\n- **#1 `wordWrap`:** Long words are cut into pieces of exactly `width` characters. Blank-line-separated paragraphs are wrapped separately and rejoined with one blank line. The output has no leading or trailing empty line.\n- **#2 `truncate`:** Length is counted in code points, and the ellipsis counts toward `max`. Whitespace before the ellipsis is removed. If the ellipsis alone is `max` or longer, only the ellipsis is returned, cut to `max` code points.\n- **#3 CSV:** `parseCSVLine` now handles quoted commas, `\"\"` escapes and empty fields. I added `parseCSV`, which handles `\\n` and `\\r\\n` row endings and quoted line breaks, and creates no empty trailing row. It is exported from `src/index.js`.\n- **#4 and #5 `formatTable`:**\n  - Ragged rows are padded out to the longest row.\n  - Numeric columns are right-aligned, including the header cell.\n  - `{ header: true }` adds the separator line and excludes the header from the numeric check.\n  - Trailing spaces are trimmed from every line. A short row therefore ends with its last column separator, for example `d |   |`.\n- **#6 `pluralize`:** I implemented the vowel/consonant `y` rule, the `s/x/z/ch/sh` → `es` rule and the seven irregular nouns, plus capitalisation. Only counts 1 and -1 give the singular.\n- **#7 `render`:** Output is HTML-escaped by default, `{{{raw}}}` is unescaped, and dotted paths and `|default` work. Missing values render as an empty string, and spaces inside the braces are allowed.\n- **#8 `levenshtein`:** Empty strings give the other string's length. I added the `ignoreCase` and `maxDistance` options, and the distance calculation stops early once `maxDistance` is exceeded.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
